    "theory": {
      "summary": "Crisp 2/4 Baroque musette in D Major contrasting an octave drone bass with agile right-hand leaps.",
      "pattern_tip": "Anchor the left-hand D2-D3 octave bounce on autopilot while your right hand outlines D major (D-F#-A) and A7 (A-C#-E).",
      "technique_tip": "Keep the 8th-note drone light and buoyant; let the top notes of the right-hand leaps ring clearly.",
      "ballade_link": "Develops 2/4 rhythmic precision and clean hand-independence over repeating bass pedals."
    }
  },
